  [longreach]    an early-tier primitive carried across many tiers to this node
OUTPUT roles:
  [birth]        the object is created / born at this section/subsection box
  [route]        parent-level typed boundary output exposed downstream
NOTE: tags are metadata only; the diagram/closure parser strips " [role]" exactly as it
strips " longreach". No wire is untagged: silence has no meaning in this scaffold.
Parent summary boxes declare paper section/component boundary I/O, not merely
next-box arrows. Section openings and output paragraphs are the authority for
parent boundary I/O; section namespaces give the finer internal birth/read/
construction structure. Tables and appendices are audit aids, not boundary
