/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE BATCH SCAFFOLD
================================================================================

EVERY EXECUTABLE BOX
Every box, sub-box, and sub-sub-box with owned mathematics has one designated
public state-shape theorem.  An existing theorem is used when its signature and
proof already express the exact transformation owned by the box.

CANONICAL SEMANTIC BANNER LANGUAGE
The file uses the following banner titles uniformly.

  EXECUTABLE BOX
    A metadata-declared box, sub-box, or sub-sub-box that owns definitions,
    lemmas, or a public constructor theorem.

  STATE-SHAPE BATCH
    The public state transformation of one executable box.

  STATE-SHAPE PARENT BATCH
    A parent composition that calls the designated child-box theorems.

  ROUTE COMPARTMENT
    A non-box bridge that composes or retains states between executable boxes.

  THEOREM-SOURCE PAYLOAD COMPARTMENT
    Shared typed source vocabulary carried by an exact retained state.

  INTERNAL BOX LEMMA
    A helper theorem owned by one executable box and not exposed as a separate
    metadata box.

  BOUNDARY INPUT SIGNATURE
    A typed section-entry frontier, not an additional executable box.

  SECTION EXECUTABLE BOX GROUP
    A descriptive section-level grouping of several executable boxes.

Qualifiers such as exact finite core, clipping, projection, exit, pass number,
or definitional packaging belong in the prose inside the banner rather than in
its title.

BATCH HEADER
The designated theorem is preceded by:

  Incoming state shape:
  Outgoing state shape:
  Effect:
  Public theorem:

The header describes the executable theorem.  It is not itself a route token.

DIRECT HANDOFF
The next batch consumes the exact proof term produced by the preceding batch.
Selected witnesses, sequences, orientations, masses, and other shared objects
are produced once and reused with the same explicit parameters.

BLOCK-MATH INTEGRITY
The outgoing state is constructed by the mathematics owned by the box.  The
named constructor lemmas occur in the transitive proof dependency of the public
theorem.  An unused theorem call does not count.

NO SKIPPING
A parent or route theorem composes every designated public theorem on the route
it claims to implement.  A box whose advertised output has no executable
producer is reported as a paper-specification blocker rather than bypassed or filled with a dummy
state.

NO ANCESTRY PACKING
An output does not copy its entire ancestry merely to make wiring visible.
Earlier facts are retained separately only when the metadata declares a read,
coherence, permission, pairing, source, or longreach role.

METADATA AUTHORITY
The existing input/output metadata and edge roles remain the connection map.
The state-shape header explains the mathematical transformation and does not
create a second downstream-consumer ledger.

EXACT SEMANTICS
The Effect line states the actual mathematical change performed by the box,
not merely a generic category label.

PAPER SOURCE COMPONENTS
Section 3 contains theorem-source components whose public output is pointwise
even though their proofs use an unbounded sequence and subsequence extraction.
The sequence diagnostics belong inside the proof of that source component.
They are not additional public inputs to the later pointwise route.

A local theorem may accept orientation, mass, scale, classification, or
reconstruction-source outputs when the paper assigns them to an established
theorem-source component. Such a theorem is a legal intermediate state
transformation. It need not be closed from the original count violation at the
same declaration site.

PARALLEL FRONTIERS
The pair-ratio frontier and atomization are parallel constructions from the same
five-divisor witness. Pair-gap controls are retained for the expanded
extraction source, but they are not constructors of the atom model and are not
used to prove triangle consistency.

TEST POLICY
This file separates three different proof statuses.

  1. A legal fixed-witness route test, where every input is produced from the
     original count violation and the same selected witness.

  2. A local sequence-classifier diagnostic, where the coherent sequence packet
     may be supplied explicitly even though
     `derive_external_violation_sequence_state` now produces that packet from
     `ExternalInfiniteViolations`.

  3. A bounded-branch component diagnostic, where analytic and theorem-source
     states are explicit inputs because their producer theorems are not yet
     connected.

Only the first item is a closed route test.  The latter two test local theorem
composition and must not be cited as parent-route or global closure.
================================================================================
-/

