SECTION EXECUTABLE BOX GROUP
Section 7.3

The first sub-layer is parameter-free finite rational algebra.  It creates one
reusable theorem packet containing exactly the two upper-saturation lemmas.

The second sub-layer joins that packet with the exact max-linear profile
already retained by Section 7.2 and adds the elementary maximum-read bounds.
It does not use profile balance, select a comparison case, or assume any
coordinate is nonnegative.

The subsection parent preserves the parallel Section 7.2 branches and adds the
two Section 7.3 outputs for their later classification consumers.
================================================================================
-/

/--
The reusable two-term and three-term upper-saturation theorem packet.
-/
/-
================================================================================
EXECUTABLE BOX
Section 7.3, Sub-layer 01, Sub-box 01
Birth token: saturation_lemmas

This executable box proves the parameter-free two-term and three-term rational
upper-saturation packet.
================================================================================
-/

def saturation_lemmas : Prop :=
  (∀ M x y : ℚ,
    x ≤ M →
      y ≤ M →
        x + y = 2 * M →
          x = M ∧ y = M) ∧
    ∀ M x y z : ℚ,
      x ≤ M →
        y ≤ M →
          z ≤ M →
            x + y + z = 3 * M →
              x = M ∧ y = M ∧ z = M

/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE BATCH
Section 7.3, Sub-layer 01, Sub-box 01

Incoming state shape:
  no retained state input

Outgoing state shape:
  saturation_lemmas

Effect:
  Proves the two-term and three-term rational upper-saturation lemmas as one
  reusable finite-algebra packet.  No max-linear profile or branch state is
  read.

Public theorem:
  build_saturation_lemmas
================================================================================
-/

theorem build_saturation_lemmas :
    saturation_lemmas := by
  constructor

  · intro M x y hx hy hsum
    constructor <;> linarith

  · intro M x y z hx hy hz hsum
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> linarith

/--
The maximum-read packet attached to one exact retained max-linear profile.

The first two conjuncts retain the precise input states.  The remaining four
conjuncts are exactly the three-entry upper bound, four-entry upper bound, and
the two binary maximum read rules from the paper.
-/
/-
================================================================================
EXECUTABLE BOX
Section 7.3, Sub-layer 02, Sub-box 02
Birth token: max_read_bounds

This executable box joins the saturation packet with the exact profile and
adds the elementary maximum-read bounds.
================================================================================
-/

def max_read_bounds
    (GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile)
    (sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence)
    (GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence) : Prop :=
  saturation_lemmas ∧
    max_linear_profile GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq ∧
    (∀ M x y z : ℚ,
      x ≤ M →
        y ≤ M →
          z ≤ M →
            maxLinearMax3 x y z ≤ M) ∧
    (∀ M w x y z : ℚ,
      w ≤ M →
        x ≤ M →
          y ≤ M →
            z ≤ M →
              maxLinearMax4 w x y z ≤ M) ∧
    (∀ x y : ℚ,
      y ≤ x →
        max x y = x) ∧
    ∀ x y : ℚ,
      x ≤ y →
        max x y = y

/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE BATCH
Section 7.3, Sub-layer 02, Sub-box 02

Incoming state shape:
  saturation_lemmas
  max_linear_profile GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Outgoing state shape:
  max_read_bounds GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Effect:
  Retains both exact inputs and adds the elementary three-entry and four-entry
  maximum upper bounds together with the two binary maximum read rules.  It
  does not invoke profile balance or perform the finite comparison split.

Public theorem:
  build_max_read_bounds
================================================================================
-/

theorem build_max_read_bounds
    {GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile}
    {sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence}
    {GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence}
    (hSaturation :
      saturation_lemmas)
    (hProfile :
      max_linear_profile
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq) :
    max_read_bounds
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq := by
  refine
    ⟨hSaturation, hProfile,
      ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩

  · intro M x y z hx hy hz
    change max x (max y z) ≤ M
    exact max_le hx (max_le hy hz)

  · intro M w x y z hw hx hy hz
    change max w (max x (max y z)) ≤ M
    exact max_le hw (max_le hx (max_le hy hz))

  · intro x y hyx
    apply le_antisymm
    · exact max_le le_rfl hyx
    · exact le_max_left x y

  · intro x y hxy
    apply le_antisymm
    · exact max_le hxy le_rfl
    · exact le_max_right x y

/--
The Section 7.3 frontier preserves every still-live Section 7.2 state and adds
the two finite-algebra outputs.

The exact profile is still available through
`refined_branch_alternatives`.  The separate saturation packet and maximum-read
packet are both retained because the balanced classification metadata consumes
both of them.
-/
def section_7_3_frontier
    (opening : CanonicalIntervalOverloadOpeningData)
    (GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile)
    (nuSeq : IncidentGrowthExponentSequence)
    (sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence)
    (GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence) : Prop :=
  I_grow opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq ∧
    refined_branch_alternatives
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq ∧
    profile_balance GSeq ∧
    saturation_lemmas ∧
    max_read_bounds
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE PARENT BATCH
Section 7.3 parent

Incoming state shape:
  section_7_2_frontier
    opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Outgoing state shape:
  section_7_3_frontier
    opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Effect:
  Builds the parameter-free saturation packet, projects the exact
  max-linear-profile state from the retained branch-alternative interface,
  builds the maximum-read packet, and retains all earlier sibling states for
  the later comparison and balanced-classification routes.

Public theorem:
  close_incident_growth_section_7_3
================================================================================
-/

theorem close_incident_growth_section_7_3
    {opening : CanonicalIntervalOverloadOpeningData}
    {GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile}
    {nuSeq : IncidentGrowthExponentSequence}
    {sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence}
    {GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence}
    (hSection72 :
      section_7_2_frontier
        opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq) :
    section_7_3_frontier
      opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq := by
  have hSaturation :
      saturation_lemmas :=
    build_saturation_lemmas

  have hProfile :
      max_linear_profile
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq :=
    hSection72.2.1.1

  have hMaxReadBounds :
      max_read_bounds
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq :=
    build_max_read_bounds
      hSaturation hProfile

  exact
    ⟨hSection72.1,
      hSection72.2.1,
      hSection72.2.2,
      hSaturation,
      hMaxReadBounds⟩

/- ## Sub-container 7.4: The finite max-linear comparison split. -/

/- Sub-layer 01 -/
/-
Paper ref: 7.4
Sub-box Label: `Exhaustive max-linear comparison split: five relative-order cases for G=(a,b,c,d)`
Sub-inputs: `max_linear_profile`
Sub-outputs: `max_linear_comparison_split`
Note: This is pure finite order bookkeeping; balance is used later in 7.5.
-/
def incident_growth_section_7_4_sub_layer_01_sub_box_01_label : String := "Exhaustive max-linear comparison split: five relative-order cases for G=(a,b,c,d)"
def incident_growth_section_7_4_sub_layer_01_sub_box_01_inputs : List String := ["max_linear_profile [construction]"]
def incident_growth_section_7_4_sub_layer_01_sub_box_01_outputs : List String := ["max_linear_comparison_split [birth]"]


/-
================================================================================
SECTION EXECUTABLE BOX GROUP
Section 7.4

This subsection is pure finite order bookkeeping for the exact max-linear
profile retained earlier.  It does not consume profile balance, saturation,
maximum-read bounds, endpoint equations, sector laws, rank data, prefix data,
affine data, or terminal data.

The child batch therefore steps back to the precise earlier state named by the
metadata:

  max_linear_profile GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

and produces the five-way comparison split for that same `GSeq`.

The subsection parent is responsible only for projecting that exact profile
from the current Section 7.3 frontier and then retaining every still-live
parallel state beside the new comparison split.
================================================================================
-/

/-- First endpoint dominance for one rational max-linear profile. -/
/-
================================================================================
EXECUTABLE BOX
Section 7.4, Sub-layer 01, Sub-box 01
Birth token: max_linear_comparison_split

This executable box performs the finite five-way relative-order split for the
exact retained max-linear profile.
================================================================================
-/

def first_endpoint_dominance
    (G : MaxLinearProfile) : Prop :=
  G 1 ≤ G 0 ∧
    G 2 ≤ G 0 ∧
    G 3 ≤ G 0

/-- Second-coordinate strict dominance for one rational profile. -/
def second_strict_dominance
    (G : MaxLinearProfile) : Prop :=
  G 0 < G 1 ∧
    G 2 < G 1 ∧
    G 3 < G 1

/-- Third-coordinate strict dominance for one rational profile. -/
def third_strict_dominance
    (G : MaxLinearProfile) : Prop :=
  G 0 < G 2 ∧
    G 1 < G 2 ∧
    G 3 < G 2

/-- Fourth endpoint dominance for one rational max-linear profile. -/
def fourth_endpoint_dominance
    (G : MaxLinearProfile) : Prop :=
  G 0 ≤ G 3 ∧
    G 1 ≤ G 3 ∧
    G 2 ≤ G 3

/-- The central tie comparison case for one rational profile. -/
def central_tie_comparison
    (G : MaxLinearProfile) : Prop :=
  G 0 ≤ G 1 ∧
    G 1 = G 2 ∧
    G 3 ≤ G 1

/--
The exhaustive comparison split attached to the exact retained max-linear
profile.

The first conjunct retains the input profile state.  The second conjunct is
only the pointwise five-way order disjunction.  No balance equation or branch
classification conclusion is present.
-/
def max_linear_comparison_split
    (GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile)
    (sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence)
    (GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence) : Prop :=
  max_linear_profile GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq ∧
    ∀ m : ℕ,
      first_endpoint_dominance (GSeq m) ∨
        second_strict_dominance (GSeq m) ∨
        third_strict_dominance (GSeq m) ∨
        fourth_endpoint_dominance (GSeq m) ∨
        central_tie_comparison (GSeq m)

/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE BATCH
Section 7.4, Sub-layer 01, Sub-box 01

Incoming state shape:
  max_linear_profile GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Outgoing state shape:
  max_linear_comparison_split GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Effect:
  Retains the exact max-linear profile and proves the exhaustive five-way
  relative-order split pointwise.  It does not read profile balance,
  saturation lemmas, maximum-read bounds, or any later route data.

Public theorem:
  build_max_linear_comparison_split
================================================================================
-/

theorem build_max_linear_comparison_split
    {GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile}
    {sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence}
    {GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence}
    (hProfile :
      max_linear_profile
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq) :
    max_linear_comparison_split
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq := by
  refine ⟨hProfile, ?_⟩
  intro m

  let a : ℚ := GSeq m 0
  let b : ℚ := GSeq m 1
  let c : ℚ := GSeq m 2
  let d : ℚ := GSeq m 3

  suffices
      (b ≤ a ∧ c ≤ a ∧ d ≤ a) ∨
        (a < b ∧ c < b ∧ d < b) ∨
        (a < c ∧ b < c ∧ d < c) ∨
        (a ≤ d ∧ b ≤ d ∧ c ≤ d) ∨
        (a ≤ b ∧ b = c ∧ d ≤ b) by
    simpa [
      first_endpoint_dominance,
      second_strict_dominance,
      third_strict_dominance,
      fourth_endpoint_dominance,
      central_tie_comparison,
      a, b, c, d
    ] using this

  by_cases hFirst :
      b ≤ a ∧ c ≤ a ∧ d ≤ a
  · exact Or.inl hFirst

  by_cases hFourth :
      a ≤ d ∧ b ≤ d ∧ c ≤ d
  · exact
      Or.inr
        (Or.inr
          (Or.inr
            (Or.inl hFourth)))

  rcases lt_trichotomy b c with hbc | hbc | hcb

  · have hac : a < c := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hca : c ≤ a :=
        le_of_not_gt hnot
      have hba : b ≤ a :=
        le_trans (le_of_lt hbc) hca
      by_cases hda : d ≤ a
      · exact hFirst ⟨hba, hca, hda⟩
      · have had : a < d :=
          lt_of_not_ge hda
        have hcd : c ≤ d :=
          le_trans hca (le_of_lt had)
        have hbd : b ≤ d :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hbc) hcd
        exact
          hFourth
            ⟨le_of_lt had, hbd, hcd⟩

    have hdc : d < c := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hcd : c ≤ d :=
        le_of_not_gt hnot
      have hbd : b ≤ d :=
        le_trans (le_of_lt hbc) hcd
      by_cases had : a ≤ d
      · exact hFourth ⟨had, hbd, hcd⟩
      · have hda : d < a :=
          lt_of_not_ge had
        have hca : c ≤ a :=
          le_trans hcd (le_of_lt hda)
        have hba : b ≤ a :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hbc) hca
        exact
          hFirst
            ⟨hba, hca, le_of_lt hda⟩

    exact
      Or.inr
        (Or.inr
          (Or.inl
            ⟨hac, hbc, hdc⟩))

  · have hab : a ≤ b := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hba : b < a :=
        lt_of_not_ge hnot
      have hca : c ≤ a := by
        rw [← hbc]
        exact le_of_lt hba
      by_cases hda : d ≤ a
      · exact
          hFirst
            ⟨le_of_lt hba, hca, hda⟩
      · have had : a < d :=
          lt_of_not_ge hda
        have hbd : b ≤ d :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hba) (le_of_lt had)
        have hcd : c ≤ d := by
          rw [← hbc]
          exact hbd
        exact
          hFourth
            ⟨le_of_lt had, hbd, hcd⟩

    have hdb : d ≤ b := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hbd : b < d :=
        lt_of_not_ge hnot
      have hcd : c ≤ d := by
        rw [← hbc]
        exact le_of_lt hbd
      by_cases had : a ≤ d
      · exact
          hFourth
            ⟨had, le_of_lt hbd, hcd⟩
      · have hda : d < a :=
          lt_of_not_ge had
        have hba : b ≤ a :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hbd) (le_of_lt hda)
        have hca : c ≤ a := by
          rw [← hbc]
          exact hba
        exact
          hFirst
            ⟨hba, hca, le_of_lt hda⟩

    exact
      Or.inr
        (Or.inr
          (Or.inr
            (Or.inr
              ⟨hab, hbc, hdb⟩)))

  · have hab : a < b := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hba : b ≤ a :=
        le_of_not_gt hnot
      have hca : c ≤ a :=
        le_trans (le_of_lt hcb) hba
      by_cases hda : d ≤ a
      · exact hFirst ⟨hba, hca, hda⟩
      · have had : a < d :=
          lt_of_not_ge hda
        have hbd : b ≤ d :=
          le_trans hba (le_of_lt had)
        have hcd : c ≤ d :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hcb) hbd
        exact
          hFourth
            ⟨le_of_lt had, hbd, hcd⟩

    have hdb : d < b := by
      by_contra hnot
      have hbd : b ≤ d :=
        le_of_not_gt hnot
      have hcd : c ≤ d :=
        le_trans (le_of_lt hcb) hbd
      by_cases had : a ≤ d
      · exact hFourth ⟨had, hbd, hcd⟩
      · have hda : d < a :=
          lt_of_not_ge had
        have hba : b ≤ a :=
          le_trans hbd (le_of_lt hda)
        have hca : c ≤ a :=
          le_trans (le_of_lt hcb) hba
        exact
          hFirst
            ⟨hba, hca, le_of_lt hda⟩

    exact
      Or.inr
        (Or.inl
          ⟨hab, hcb, hdb⟩)

/--
The Section 7.4 frontier preserves all still-live Section 7.3 branches and
adds the comparison split as a new sibling state.

The comparison split does not absorb balance or the saturation packets.  Those
states remain separate because Section 7.5 combines them only after this pure
order split has been completed.
-/
def section_7_4_frontier
    (opening : CanonicalIntervalOverloadOpeningData)
    (GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile)
    (nuSeq : IncidentGrowthExponentSequence)
    (sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence)
    (GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence) : Prop :=
  I_grow opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq ∧
    refined_branch_alternatives
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq ∧
    profile_balance GSeq ∧
    saturation_lemmas ∧
    max_read_bounds
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq ∧
    max_linear_comparison_split
      GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

/-
================================================================================
STATE-SHAPE PARENT BATCH
Section 7.4 parent

Incoming state shape:
  section_7_3_frontier
    opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Outgoing state shape:
  section_7_4_frontier
    opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq

Effect:
  Projects only the exact `max_linear_profile` state required by the Section
  7.4 child batch, builds the pure five-way order split, and retains I_grow,
  refined branch alternatives, profile balance, saturation lemmas, and
  maximum-read bounds unchanged for their later parallel use.

Public theorem:
  close_incident_growth_section_7_4
================================================================================
-/

theorem close_incident_growth_section_7_4
    {opening : CanonicalIntervalOverloadOpeningData}
    {GammaSeq : Gamma_W_adjacent_growth_profile}
    {nuSeq : IncidentGrowthExponentSequence}
    {sigmaSeq : ProfileReadSequence}
    {GSeq : MaxLinearProfileSequence}
    (hSection73 :
      section_7_3_frontier
        opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq) :
    section_7_4_frontier
      opening GammaSeq nuSeq sigmaSeq GSeq := by
  have hProfile :
      max_linear_profile
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq :=
    hSection73.2.1.1

  have hComparisonSplit :
      max_linear_comparison_split
        GammaSeq sigmaSeq GSeq :=
    build_max_linear_comparison_split
      hProfile

  exact
    ⟨hSection73.1,
      hSection73.2.1,
      hSection73.2.2.1,
      hSection73.2.2.2.1,
      hSection73.2.2.2.2,
      hComparisonSplit⟩

