STATE-SHAPE BATCH
Section 9.1, Sub-layer 03, Sub-box 03

Incoming state shape:
  regular_coloring_problem C nSeq dSeq opening
  degree_two_branch_family C nSeq dSeq opening

Outgoing state shape:
  regular_coloring_alternatives C nSeq dSeq opening

Effect:
  Retains both exact predecessor batches and attaches the handshake
  classification to the same source-tied coloring datum.  The output says only
  monochrome or one compatible member of C_2(chi).  It does not eliminate the
  degree-two route and does not choose the post-prefix survivor.

Public theorem:
  build_regular_coloring_alternatives
================================================================================
-/

theorem build_regular_coloring_alternatives
    {C : ℝ}
    {nSeq : ℕ → ℕ}
    {dSeq : ℕ → Fin 5 → ℕ}
    {opening : CanonicalIntervalOverloadOpeningData}
    (hRegular :
      regular_coloring_problem C nSeq dSeq opening)
    (hFamily :
      degree_two_branch_family C nSeq dSeq opening) :
    regular_coloring_alternatives C nSeq dSeq opening := by
  refine ⟨hRegular, hFamily, ?_⟩
  intro data _hSource hRegularAt hFamilyAt
  exact
    classify_regular_coloring_at
      data hRegularAt hFamilyAt


